Wallpaper redistribution notice for the scoot looks shipped in this image
(`rootfs/defaults/scoot-looks/`). A published Docker image is redistribution,
so these terms apply to every copy of selkies-nix-webtop-scoot pulled from a
registry, not just to this source tree. Nothing below is covered by this
repository's GPL-3.0 license; each image stays under its own license.

- `radial-burst/wallpaper.png` is "Colorful radial lines exploding on a dark
  background" by Sufyan pir, published on Unsplash on June 18, 2026
  (https://unsplash.com/illustrations/colorful-radial-lines-exploding-on-a-dark-background-ETTtKnva9MM).
  Free to use under the Unsplash License (https://unsplash.com/license):
  downloading, copying, modifying and distributing it -- including
  commercially and without attribution -- is allowed, but compiling images to
  build a similar or competing service is not. Credit in scoot's NOTICE and
  docs/examples/radial-burst/README.md is a courtesy. Source: scoot's
  docs/assets/wallpapers/radial-burst.png (scoot-sh/scoot, checked against
  scoot main 39c3a5e1, 2026-10-04).

- `music-desk/wallpaper.png` is "Musical instruments and audio equipment on a
  white surface" by Alghozy (@artgho), published on Unsplash
  (https://unsplash.com/illustrations/musical-instruments-and-audio-equipment-on-a-white-surface-b6Us5E-BO8w).
  Same Unsplash License terms as above. Source: scoot's
  docs/assets/wallpapers/music-desk.png (scoot-sh/scoot, same rev).

- `vinyl-sunset/` ships NO wallpaper image, deliberately. Its illustration
  ("Lofi, vintage, vinyl, study, audio" by AninditaErina, marked AI-generated:
  https://pixabay.com/illustrations/lofi-vintage-vinyl-study-audio-8390965/)
  is under the Pixabay Content License
  (https://pixabay.com/service/license/), which forbids passing the content
  on standalone, substantially as it exists on Pixabay. The look's
  `[wallpaper]` is the illustration's own espresso (#271A1F) instead. To see
  the real illustration, download it yourself from Pixabay and point your
  ~/.config/scoot/config.toml [wallpaper] image at your copy. No wallhaven
  or Chillhop image is used anywhere in this image.

The `.toml`, `.ini`, `.yml`, `.css`, `.sh` and `.theme` look files are adapted
from scoot's docs/examples/vinyl-sunset, docs/examples/music-desk and
docs/examples/radial-burst (scoot-sh/scoot, MIT); each file's header says what
this image changed and why.
